[?2004l[?2004h>         "status": "ANSWERED",
[?2004l[?2004h>         "answer": "The safety risks listed for Paxlovid include: serious, life-threatening, or fatal adverse reactions due to drug interactions; hypersensitivity reactions (including anaphylaxis, toxic epidermal necrolysis, Stevens-Johnson syndrome, and malaise); hepatotoxicity (hepatic transaminase elevations, clinical hepatitis, jaundice); risk of HIV-1 resistance development in individuals with uncontrolled or undiagnosed HIV-1 infection; and common adverse reactions from clinical trials (incidence >=1% and greater than placebo) which are dysgeusia (5% vs <1% placebo) and diarrhea (3% vs 2% placebo). Other adverse reactions identified under Emergency Use Authorization include headache, hypertension, abdominal pain, nausea, vomiting, and malaise.",
