      Quote: 'Initiation of lopinavir and ritonavir, a CYP3A inhibitor, in patients receiving medications metabolized by CYP3A or initiation of medications metabolized by CYP3A in patients already receiving lopinavir\xa0and ritonavir, may increase plasma concentrations of medications metabolized by CYP3A.'
    - PASSAGE_0015 (5.2 Toxicity in Preterm Neonates)
      Quote: 'Preterm neonates may be at increased risk of propylene glycol-associated adverse events due to diminished ability to metabolize propylene glycol, thereby leading to accumulation and potential adverse events.'
    - PASSAGE_0016 (5.3 Pancreatitis)
      Quote: 'Pancreatitis has been observed in patients receiving lopinavir\xa0and ritonavir therapy, including those who developed marked triglyceride elevations.'
    - PASSAGE_0017 (5.4 Hepatotoxicity)
      Quote: 'There have been postmarketing reports of hepatic dysfunction, including some fatalities. These have generally occurred in patients with advanced HIV-1 disease taking multiple concomitant medications in the setting of underlying chronic hepatitis or cirrhosis.'
    - PASSAGE_0018 (5.5 QT Interval Prolongation)
      Quote: 'Postmarketing cases of QT interval prolongation and torsade de pointes have been reported although causality of lopinavir\xa0and ritonavir could not be established.'
    - PASSAGE_0019 (5.6 PR Interval Prolongation)
      Quote: 'Lopinavir\xa0and ritonavir prolongs the PR interval in some patients. Cases of second or third degree atrioventricular block have been reported.'
    - PASSAGE_0022 (5.9 Lipid Elevations)
      Quote: 'Treatment with lopinavir\xa0and ritonavir has resulted in large increases in the concentration of total cholesterol and triglycerides .'

