    - PASSAGE_0014 (5.1 Risk of Serious Adverse Reactions Due to Drug Interactions)
      Quote: 'Initiation of lopinavir and ritonavir, a CYP3A inhibitor, in patients receiving medications metabolized by CYP3A or initiation of medications metabolized by CYP3A in patients already receiving lopinavir\xa0and ritonavir, may increase plasma concentrations of medications metabolized by CYP3A.'
    - PASSAGE_0015 (5.2 Toxicity in Preterm Neonates)
      Quote: 'Lopinavir\xa0and ritonavir oral solution should not be used in preterm neonates in the immediate postnatal period because of possible toxicities.'
    - PASSAGE_0016 (5.3 Pancreatitis)
      Quote: 'Pancreatitis should be considered if clinical symptoms (nausea, vomiting, abdominal pain) or abnormalities in laboratory values (such as increased serum lipase or amylase values) suggestive of pancreatitis occur.'
    - PASSAGE_0017 (5.4 Hepatotoxicity)
      Quote: 'Appropriate laboratory testing should be conducted prior to initiating therapy with lopinavir\xa0and ritonavir and patients should be monitored closely during treatment.'
    - PASSAGE_0018 (5.5 QT Interval Prolongation)
      Quote: 'Avoid use in patients with congenital long QT syndrome, those with hypokalemia, and with other drugs that prolong the QT interval .'
    - PASSAGE_0019 (5.6 PR Interval Prolongation)
      Quote: 'Lopinavir\xa0and ritonavir should be used with caution in patients with underlying structural heart disease, pre-existing conduction system abnormalities, ischemic heart disease or cardiomyopathies'
    - PASSAGE_0022 (5.9 Lipid Elevations)
      Quote: 'Triglyceride and cholesterol testing should be performed prior to initiating lopinavir\xa0and ritonavir therapy and at periodic intervals during therapy.'

